{
 "_why": "Everyday words put first, where the join through English picks a rarer sense or misses (same role as COMMON in build_vidict.py). Vietnamese function words read the Vietnamese way: cái đó = that thing, cái quái gì = what on earth, thế/vậy = then (2026-10-15). es đi was hacer (make): ir. ja ăn was 食う (rude), sống was ある; về was 작동하다/那么 (2026-10-15 sweep). ko giúp was 지원하다 (apply, support). đừng was 떽 (ko), な/せん (ja); đừng sợ / đừng lo as said (2026-10-15). zh đến/vào, ja/fr làm: the everyday verb first (sweep of đừng, 2026-10-15). ko cô/anh/chị gave 당신 first (cold or rude spoken to someone; cô also 나): 그쪽 and the kin word; ông/bà 어르신. es ngồi was sentar (seat someone): sentarse. có sao không / không sao as said (cô có sao không gave 있다 왜 아니요). ja cô/anh/chị/bạn/ông/bà gave あなた first: そちら, the kin word, 君 for the familiar ones. en: the English list is the pivot itself; the function words and pronouns are as spoken (cô = you, là = is) (2026-10-15). en top verbs whose first sense was another word (sống = spine, thành = into, ghét = dirt): the verb (sweep, 2026-10-15).",
